    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-ceiling power threats: **Yordan Alvarez** (76.23) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84). **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a favorable matchup against Colin Rea, where his elite xwOBA of 0.419 and a prime #3 batting position make him the safest bet for run production. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** draws a premium matchup against Roki Sasaki; despite the tough nature of the opposing pitcher, the +13% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage makes him our highest-projected outfielder. **Trea Turner** (71.06) remains a focal point for our roster construction, as the combination of his #1 spot in the order and the slow delivery of Slade Cecconi provides an opportunistic window for the stolen bases that are vital to our 5x5 strategy.\n\nWe are keeping a close eye on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (65.81), whose score is buoyed significantly by a +14% dynamic platoon advantage against Kai-Wei Teng. Conversely, **Kazuma Okamoto** (43.02) represents our most volatile start; he draws a challenging assignment against Paul Skenes, whose skill level imposes a -19% penalty on our base projections. The most difficult bench decision involved **Casey Schmitt** (50.65), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Casey Schmitt** offers some utility against left-handed pitching, he lacked the efficiency scores required to displace our current starters. We continue to monitor the status of **Junior Caminero**, who remains benched due to a rainout. With multiple lineups still officially \"Pending,\" managers must remain vigilant for defensive switches that could depress the value of **Gary Sanchez** or **Dillon Dingler**, particularly if their projected batting positions drift lower in the order.",
